With a budget too small to finish the object:
  attempt 1: finish_reason=length, 35 chars
             rejected: response was truncated before it finished
  attempt 2: finish_reason=stop, 37 chars
  -> payment_days=60 price_cap_pct=3  after 2 attempt(s)

With a sensible budget:
  attempt 1: finish_reason=stop, 37 chars
  -> payment_days=60 price_cap_pct=3  after 1 attempt(s)

Three layers, and each catches what the one below cannot:
  the strict schema   guarantees the shape
  Pydantic bounds     guarantee the values are in range
  a field validator   guarantees they are sensible for your business

None of them helps with truncation, which arrives as valid-looking nothing.
finish_reason is the only signal, exactly as Chapter 4 warned.
